# The same post, with the wait started by the post itself.
dispatcher: dispatcher pane\n`crew reply worker:<branch> "<directive>"` {
  shape: rectangle
}
reply: crew/internal/reply.Run\nappends the msg, then nudgeAfter() {
  shape: rectangle
  style.stroke: "#2E7D32"
}
bus: crew bus log\nevents.jsonl {
  shape: storage
}
gate: nudgeAfter's checks\n--no-nudge · role: · remote host · engine {
  shape: rectangle
  style.stroke: "#2E7D32"
}
engine: nudge.EngineOf\ndispatch/resume row's engine {
  shape: rectangle
  style.stroke: "#2E7D32"
}
spawn: reply.DetachedNudge\nown session, /dev/null, nudge-wait.log {
  shape: rectangle
  style.stroke: "#2E7D32"
}
wait: crew nudge --wait\narm.wait(), one lock per lead {
  shape: rectangle
}
lead: idle claude/pi lead pane {
  shape: rectangle
}
skip: stderr `reply: no nudge (<reason>)`\nstdout stays empty {
  shape: text
  style.stroke: "#2E7D32"
}

dispatcher -> reply: posts the directive
reply -> bus: bus.Append(msg)
reply -> gate: a local worker got the msg
engine -> gate: claude/pi only
gate -> spawn: started, and returns at once
gate -> skip: nothing started, why
spawn -> wait: `nudge --crew <id> --wait -- <sid>`
wait -> lead: types `crew inbox "$CREW_WORKER_ID"` when idle
wait -> wait: a second reply's wait joins the same lock
